'''Calvin Lawrence Booth''' (born May 7, 1976) is a former [[National Basketball Association|NBA]] basketball player and team executive who most recently served as the [[General manager (basketball)|general manager]] of the [[Denver Nuggets]].<ref>{{Cite news|url=https://www.nba.com/nuggets/news/nuggets-calvin-booth-general-manager-070720|title=Calvin Booth Named General Manager|date=July 7, 2020 |website=NBA.com|access-date=July 10, 2020}}</ref>   He played 10 seasons for various NBA teams as a [[center (basketball)|center]] after playing [[college basketball]] for the [[Penn State Nittany Lions basketball|Penn State Nittany Lions]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.basketball-reference.com/players/b/boothca01.html |author=Basketball-Reference |title=Calvin Booth |access-date=2025-11-19}}</ref> After his playing career concluded, he served in front office positions for the [[New Orleans Pelicans]], [[Minnesota Timberwolves]], and [[Denver Nuggets]], eventually being named [[General manager (basketball)|general manager]] of the Nuggets in 2020, a position he held until 2025.<ref name="fired">{{cite web|first=Matt|last=Brooks|title=Denver Nuggets Relieve Head Coach Michael Malone of Duties; Will Not Extend Calvin Booth |date=April 8, 2025|website=NBA.com|url=https://www.nba.com/nuggets/news/denver-nuggets-relieve-head-coach-michael-malone-of-duties-will-not-extend-calvin-booth|access-date=April 9, 2025}}</ref>

