'''Caleb Michael David Houstan''' ({{IPAc-en|ˈ|h|j|uː|s|t|ə|n}} {{respell|HEW|stən}};<ref>{{cite press release|title=2023-24 start of season NBA pronunciation guide|url=https://www.nba.com/news/2023-24-start-of-season-nba-pronunciation-guide|website=NBA.com|date=October 24, 2023|access-date=May 18, 2024}}</ref> born January 9, 2003) is a Canadian professional [[basketball]] player, who most recently played for the [[Atlanta Hawks]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He played [[college basketball]] for the [[Michigan Wolverines men's basketball|Michigan Wolverines]].

After reclassifying to graduate high school a year early, Houstan was a consensus five-star [[college recruiting|recruit]] with  [[McDonald's All-American Game|McDonald's All-American]] and [[Jordan Brand Classic]] recognition as one of the top players in the 2021 class. He won a silver medal with Canada at the [[2019 FIBA Under-16 Americas Championship]] and a bronze medal at the [[2021 FIBA Under-19 Basketball World Cup]].
